      ":question/problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -6 & 8 \\\\ -7 & 9 & 11 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{13}=0$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}.\n$$\n\nAt the requested entry, this gives\n\n$$\na_{13}=8+(1)\\cdot (-8)=0.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C &=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -6 & 8 \\\\ -7 & 9 & 11 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}11 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 9 & 11 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}.\n$$",
